3. Member who issued maximum number of books

Pehle count karenge ki har member ne kitni books issue ki.

SELECT m.member_id,
       m.member_name,
       COUNT(i.issue_id) AS total_books
FROM MEMBER m
JOIN ISSUE i
ON m.member_id = i.member_id
GROUP BY m.member_id, m.member_name
ORDER BY total_books DESC
LIMIT 1;

Logic

Sabse important part:

COUNT(i.issue_id)

→ member ne kitni baar book issue ki.

GROUP BY m.member_id, m.member_name

→ har member ka separate group.

ORDER BY total_books DESC

→ maximum count sabse upar.

LIMIT 1

→ sirf maximum wala member.

Sample mein:

Rahul → 2
Aman → 2
Shreyansh → 0

Yahan Rahul aur Aman tie hain. Upar wali query sirf ek return karegi.

Agar lab mein maximum issue karne wale saare members, including ties, dikhane hain, to:

SELECT m.member_id,
       m.member_name,
       COUNT(i.issue_id) AS total_books
FROM MEMBER m
JOIN ISSUE i
ON m.member_id = i.member_id
GROUP BY m.member_id, m.member_name
HAVING COUNT(i.issue_id) = (
    SELECT MAX(book_count)
    FROM (
        SELECT COUNT(*) AS book_count
        FROM ISSUE
        GROUP BY member_id
    ) x
);

Exam mein basic version yaad rakhna:

GROUP BY → COUNT → ORDER BY DESC → LIMIT 1


